  "moduleDigitRebusTitle": "Digit Rebuses",
  "@moduleDigitRebusTitle": {"description": "Title of Module 02."},
  "moduleDigitRebusDescription": "Every row and every column is an equation: place digits following the glyph hints.",
  "@moduleDigitRebusDescription": {"description": "Short description of Module 02, shown on its home-screen card."},
  "digitRebusListTitle": "Digit Rebuses",
  "@digitRebusListTitle": {"description": "Title of Module 02's puzzle list screen."},
  "digitRebusResetConfirmBody": "All entered digits will be removed.",
  "@digitRebusResetConfirmBody": {"description": "Body text of Module 02's reset confirmation dialog (no givens in this module)."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep1": "This is a 4×4 square: every row and every column is an equation, solved strictly left to right (top to bottom), with no operator precedence. The fourth cell is the result.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep1": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 1 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep2": "The digits are hidden behind glyphs. Each glyph admits only a few digits — the legend below the grid always shows which: a loop on top, for example, means 0, 8 or 9.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep2": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 2 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep3": "Start with row 2: (a + b) × c. The result is a single digit and the multiplier is at least 3, so a + b is at most 3: only a = 1 and b = 2 fit.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep3": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 3 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep4": "Then 1 + 2 = 3 and 3 × 3 = 9 — row 2 reads 1 + 2 × 3 = 9.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep4": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 4 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep5": "Column 1: (a − 1) × c. The multiplier is again at least 3, so a − 1 = 3, meaning a = 4 — and 3 × 3 = 9: the column reads 4 − 1 × 3 = 9.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep5": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 5 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep6": "Row 3: 3 + b + c. Of the admitted digits only 3 + 2 + 1 = 6 works.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep6": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 6 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep7": "Column 3: a − 3 − 1. Of 0, 6 and 8 only 6 works: 6 − 3 − 1 = 2.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep7": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 7 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep8": "The remaining cells follow from their rows: 4 + 8 : 6 = 2 and 9 − 3 : 2 = 3. All eight equations hold.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep8": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 8 of 9."},
  "digitRebusTutorialStep9": "Done! In the puzzles, tap a cell — the menu shows only the digits its glyph admits. Any filling where all eight equations hold wins.",
  "@digitRebusTutorialStep9": {"description": "Module 02 tutorial step 9 of 9."},
